think Two asks in one word: name the whole ecosystem, and prove the seed safe.
think The ecosystem lacked its one brand — the modules are warmly named, the whole was not. Grep-tested sheaf loam meadow furrow granary harvest pasture — all free in .rye/.brix/LEXICON except granary (already a module dir).
think Chose Sheaf: a bundle of grain stalks bound into one is exactly the ecosystem of modules bound into one Grain, and it is Grothendieck's word (a sheaf glues local data into a coherent global whole) — the maintainer named Grothendieck as an inspiration. Warm, plain, safe, gource-visualizable.
think Seated Sheaf as PROPOSED in context/LEXICON.md (awaits Keaton's word to fully seat) — a propose, not a seat, per the cell discipline.
think For the audit: a workflow is the right tool — the risk is unknown real identifiers (friends, places, companies, schools) that a known-name scrub list cannot catch; an agent reading prose recognizes what a grep list misses. Launched seed-name-audit (w34sfmeai): 8 area agents over the shipping prose (context, foundations, external-research, design, prompts, teaching, root+rules, linengrow+READMEs) each flagging real identifiers beyond the already-scrubbed maintainer, then a synthesis into a scrub/sub_exclude action list and a publish verdict.
obs The perl insert for the LEXICON entry choked on the pipe/asterisk content; the Edit tool seated it cleanly. Tool choice matters — dedicated tools over shell for structured prose.
obs Two workflows now run in the background — the docs+baton (w2ojhqiu6) and the name-audit (w34sfmeai). Both re-invoke automatically on completion; no polling needed. Per "send everything when all done," the send holds until both land.
obs The audit's findings expand the scrub/IDENT nets and sub_exclude the too-personal files, then re-project and re-run the leak scan — mechanical to apply, yet the publish verdict is Keaton's to read.
obs The docs+baton workflow (w2ojhqiu6) landed while the audit runs: SIX name-clean onboarding guides (front-door · first-hour · dev-guide · sandboxing · IDEs+agents+API · running-on-your-machines) — the publish-ready teaching face — plus the recursive next-kg baton for every quest/journey/equinox/season.
obs Independent IDENT recheck of the six manual docs (net expanded with Thacher/Sonoma/Washoe/Mycelium) returned MANUAL_DOCS_IDENT_CLEAN. The recursive baton names internal season ops (the name-debride, the pseudonym change, the shred census) — sub_excluded as a private roadmap, kin to the handoff/3x39/fusion batons.
